==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{af|ru|на-|пра́вить|t2=to govern, to rule, to drive, to steer}}.

For the meaning development compare with {{m+|la|dīrigō||to lay straight, to arrange in lines, to direct to a place, guide, steer}} (whence {{m+|en|direct}}) connected with {{m|la|regō||to rule, to govern, to direct, to guide, steer}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|напра́вить}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-направить.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|напра́вить|pf|impf=направля́ть}}

# to [[direct]]
# to [[turn]], to [[aim]], to [[level]], to [[point]]
# to [[refer]], to [[send]], to [[assign]], to [[detach]]
# to [[sharpen]]

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|pf|4a+p|напра́вить}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ru|направля́ться|g=impf}}, {{l|ru|напра́виться|g=pf}}
* {{l|ru|разнонапра́вленный}}
* {{l|ru|однонапра́вленный}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ru|направле́ние}}
